msgid "These five settings (opcache sizing plus the realpath cache) are locked in when PHP starts up, so the only way to change them is editing your real php.ini file and restarting PHP — no plugin can do it any other way, and .user.ini / .htaccess genuinely cannot reach them regardless of what’s written there. This action edits that file directly. A mistake here, or running it on a shared or live server, can bring down PHP for every site on that server until someone fixes it by hand. Only use this on a local site you fully control and can easily reinstall (Local, XAMPP, MAMP, Laragon, or your own Docker setup)."
msgstr ""

